<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hohenlinden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1800</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-second-coalition">War of the Second Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hohenlinden was fought on 3 December 1800 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>, between a French army under Jean Moreau and an Austrian and Bavarian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-john-of-austria">Archduke John</a>. Moreau's divisions caught the Austrians strung out in the forest and routed them, taking many prisoners. Coming after Marengo, the defeat forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> to make peace by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-luneville">Treaty of Lunéville</a> in 1801, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-second-coalition">War of the Second Coalition</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hohenlinden.jpg" alt="Battle of Hohenlinden" width="320" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henri Frédéric Schopin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_de_Hohenlinden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
